The north coast of the Dominican Republic is known by three names, the Green, Amber &amp; Silver Coasts: Green for the lush flora &amp; fauna along the entire coast, Amber for the rich amber deposits that flush out with the rivers, and Silver for the name Christopher Columbus gave to Puerto Plata, or Silver Port. He named it so thanks to a plant growing along the shore (Peperomia Caperata Variegate). The silver reflections from its leaves made him think there was treasure to find. In the end, he did find it. Not a treasure chest, but a land of full of green gold, and where he landed was richest of all.
