Chemical oxidation is a common and important method for preparing expandable graphite. Oxidation is the key step of preparing expandable graphite by chemical oxidation. Whether the intercalation reaction can proceed smoothly depends on the degree of opening between graphite layers. The oxidant makes the carbon atoms in adjacent layers of the graphite edge repel each other, increases the layer space, reduces the activation energy of the intercalation reaction, and creates necessary conditions for the intercalation agent to insert into the graphite layer smoothly.
